{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-isa-41-1","title":"Isaiah 41:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 God expostulates with his people, about his mercies to the church; 10 about his promises; 21 and about the vanity of idols.</p>\n<p>silence. 49:1; Ps 46:10; Hab 2:20; Zec 2:13 let the people. 6,7,21,22; 8:9,10; Job 38:3; 40:7; Joe 3:10,11 let us. 1:18; Job 23:3-7; 31:35,36; 40:8-10; Mic 6:1-3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-41-2","title":"Isaiah 41:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>Who raised. 25; 45:13; 46:11; Ge 11:31; 12:1-3; 17:1; Heb 11:8-10 the righteous man. Heb. righteousness. gave. 15; 45:1; Ge 14:14,15; Ezr 1:2; Heb 7:1 as the. 15,16; 2Sa 22:43; 2Ki 13:7 as driven. 40:24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-41-3","title":"Isaiah 41:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>safely. Heb. in peace. 57:2; Job 5:24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-41-4","title":"Isaiah 41:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>hath. 26; 40:12,26; 42:24 calling. 44:7; 46:10; 48:3-7; De 32:7,8; Ac 15:18; 17:26 I the Lord. 43:10; 44:6; 48:12; Re 1:11,17; 2:8; 22:13 with the. 46:3,4; Mt 1:23; 28:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-41-5","title":"Isaiah 41:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>isles. Ge 10:5; Eze 26:15,16 the ends. Ex 15:14; Jos 2:10; 5:1; Ps 65:8; 66:3; 67:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-41-6","title":"Isaiah 41:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>helped. 40:19; 44:12; 1Sa 4:7-9; 5:3-5; Da 3:1-7; Ac 19:24-28 of good courage. Heb. strong. 35:4; Joe 3:9-11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-41-7","title":"Isaiah 41:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>the carpenter. 40:19; 44:12-15; 46:6,7; Jer 10:3-5,9; Da 3:1-7 goldsmith. or, founder. him that smote the anvil. or, thesmiting. saying, It is ready for the soldering. or, saying of the solder, It is good. that it. 40:20; 46:7; Jud 18:17,18,24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-41-8","title":"Isaiah 41:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>thou. 43:1; 44:1,2,21; 48:12; 49:3; Ex 19:5,6; Le 25:42; De 7:6-8; 10:15 De 14:2; Ps 33:12; 105:6,42-45; 135:4; Jer 33:24 the seed. Mt 3:9; Joh 8:33-44; Ro 4:12,13; 9:4-8; Ga 3:19; 4:22-31 my friend. 2Ch 20:7; Joh 15:14,15; Jas 2:23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-41-9","title":"Isaiah 41:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>whom. 2; Jos 24:2-4; Ne 9:7-38; Ps 107:2,3; Lu 13:29; Re 5:9 called. De 7:7; 1Co 1:26-29; Jas 2:5 I have chosen. 1Sa 12:22; Ps 94:14; Jer 33:25,26; Ro 11:1,2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-41-10","title":"Isaiah 41:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>Fear. 13,14; 12:2; 43:1,5; 44:2; 51:12,13; Ge 15:1; De 20:1; 31:6-8 Jos 1:9; 2Ch 20:17; 32:8; Ps 27:1; 46:1,2,7,11; Lu 1:13,30; 2:10,11 Ro 8:31 for I am thy God. 52:7; 60:19; 1Ch 12:18; Ps 147:12; Ho 1:9; Zec 13:9; Joh 8:54,55 I will strengthen. 40:29-31; De 33:27-29; Ps 29:11; Zec 10:12; 2Co 12:9; Eph 3:16 Php 4:13 I will uphold. Ps 37:17,24; 41:12; 63:8; 145:14 the right. Ps 65:5; 89:13,14; 99:4; 144:8,11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-41-11","title":"Isaiah 41:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>all they. 45:24; 49:26; 54:17; 60:12-14; Ex 11:8; 23:22; Zec 12:3; Ac 13:8-11 Ac 16:39; Re 3:9 as nothing. 24,29; 40:17; Da 4:35 they that strive with thee. Heb. the men of thy strife.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-41-12","title":"Isaiah 41:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>shalt seek. Job 20:7-9; Ps 37:35,36 them that contended with thee. Heb. the men of thycontention. they that war against thee. Heb. the men of thy war.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-41-13","title":"Isaiah 41:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>will hold. 43:6; 45:1; 51:18; De 33:26-29; Ps 63:8; 73:23; 109:31; 2Ti 4:17 Fear. 10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-41-14","title":"Isaiah 41:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>thou worm. Job 25:6; Ps 22:6 men. or, few men. De 7:7; Mt 7:14; Lu 12:32; Ro 9:27 saith. 43:14; 44:6,24; 47:4; 48:17; 49:7,26; 54:5,8; 59:20; 60:16; 63:16 Job 19:25; Ps 19:14; Jer 50:34; Ga 3:13; Tit 2:14; Re 5:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-41-15","title":"Isaiah 41:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>I will make. 21:10; 28:27; Hab 3:12 teeth. Heb. mouths. thou shalt. Ps 18:42; Mic 4:13; Zec 4:7; 2Co 10:4,5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-41-16","title":"Isaiah 41:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>shalt fan. 17:13; Ps 1:4; Jer 15:7; 51:2; Mt 3:12 thou shalt rejoice. 12:6; 25:1-3; 45:24,25; 61:10,11; 1Sa 2:1,2; Jer 9:23,24; Hab 3:18 Lu 1:46,47; Ro 5:11; 1Co 1:30,31; Php 3:3; *Gr:</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-41-17","title":"Isaiah 41:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>the poor. 61:1; 66:2; Ps 68:9,10; 72:12,13; 102:16,17; Mt 5:3 seek. 55:1; Ex 17:3,6; Ps 42:2; 63:1,2; Am 8:11-13; Mt 5:6; Joh 4:10-15 Joh 7:37-39; Re 21:6; 22:17 their tongue. Ps 22:15; La 4:4; Lu 16:24 I the Lord. 30:19; Jud 15:18,19; Ps 34:6; 50:15; 102:17; 107:5,6; 2Co 12:9 I the God. 42:16; Ge 28:15; Ps 94:14; Heb 13:5,6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-41-18","title":"Isaiah 41:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>12:3; 30:25; 32:2; 35:6,7; 43:19,20; 44:3; 48:21; 49:9,10; 58:11 Ps 46:4; 78:15,16; 105:41; 107:35; Eze 47:1-8; Joe 3:18; Zec 14:8 Re 7:17; 22:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-41-19","title":"Isaiah 41:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>plant. 27:6; 32:15; 37:31,32; 51:3; 55:13; 60:21; 61:3,11; Ps 92:13,14 Eze 17:22-24; 47:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-41-20","title":"Isaiah 41:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>43:7-13,21; 44:23; 45:6-8; 66:18; Ex 9:16; Nu 23:23; Job 12:9 Ps 109:27; Eph 2:6-10; 2Th 1:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-41-21","title":"Isaiah 41:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>Produce. Heb. Cause to come near. Job 23:3,4; 31:37; 38:3; 40:7-9; Mic 6:1,2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-41-22","title":"Isaiah 41:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>and shew. 42:9; 43:9-12; 45:21; 48:14; Joh 13:19; 16:14 consider them. Heb. set our heart upon them.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-41-23","title":"Isaiah 41:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>that we may know. 42:9; 44:7,8; 45:8; 46:9,10; Joh 13:19; Ac 15:18 do good. 45:7; 46:7; Jer 10:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-41-24","title":"Isaiah 41:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>ye are. 29; 44:9,10; Ps 115:8; Jer 10:8,14; 51:17,18; 1Co 8:4 of nothing. or, worse than nothing. of nought. or, worsethan of a viper. an abomination. 66:24; De 7:26; 27:15; Re 17:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-41-25","title":"Isaiah 41:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>I have.Jehovah here, by the mouth of the prophet, predicts the victories of Cyrus over the Chaldeans and their allies, at least 150 years before the event, as one instance of his foreknowledge and invincible power. Media lay north of Babylon, and Persia eastward; and Cyrus commanded the forces of both these nations; and, by his wonderful success, he trampled down mighty monarchs as mortar, and as the potter treads the clay.</p>\n<p>raised. 21:2; 44:28; 45:1-6,13; 46:10,11; Jer 51:27-29 shall he call. Ezr 1:2,3 come upon. 2; 10:6; 2Sa 22:43; Mic 7:10; Zec 10:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-41-26","title":"Isaiah 41:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>declared. 22; 43:9; 44:7; 45:21; Hab 2:18-20 righteous. 23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-41-27","title":"Isaiah 41:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>first. 4; 43:10; 44:6; 48:12; Re 2:8 I will give. 40:9; 44:28; 52:7; Ezr 1:1,2; Na 1:15; Lu 2:10,11; Ro 10:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-41-28","title":"Isaiah 41:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>I beheld. 63:5; Da 2:10,11; 4:7,8; 5:8 answer. Heb. return.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-isa-41-29","title":"Isaiah 41:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"ISA","chapterStart":41,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":41,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>they are all. 24; 44:9-20; Ps 115:4-8; 135:15-18; Jer 10:2-16; Hab 2:18 wind. Jer 5:13</p>"}]}